  "final_message": "If you call `call_with_retry()` without `max_attempts`, it makes at most **4** attempts, and that count includes the first try.\n\n- In `retry.py`, a missing `max_attempts` (it defaults to `None`) falls back to `DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 4`.\n- The loop is `for _ in range(attempts)`, which calls `fn()` 4 times at most. It stops early if a call succeeds; otherwise it raises the last exception after the 4th failure.\n- `MAX_RETRIES = 3` in `decoy_network.py` and `RETRY_LIMIT = 5` in `decoy_backoff.py` have no effect, because `retry.py` doesn't import either file.\n- `main7.py` calls `call_with_retry(lambda: 1)` with no `max_attempts`, so it uses the default.\n- `.amplifier/settings.local.yaml` contains only an empty bundle setting and doesn't change this.\n\nANSWER: 4",
